{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774129906,"nonce":"MwC9wketnI3BUZ7/8UZA0vNNMNE=","message":"**Badge correction:** The notification badge on the Events sub-tab should be user-configurable — which event types contribute to the count. Auth results in particular are not a surprise to the user (they approved it themselves). The badge is useful for things like incoming work-unit assignments or continuations, but the user should control what counts.\n\n**Per-prompt parameter snapshots (keyframe model):** Store parameter state only on the first message that uses a given configuration. Subsequent messages inherit until a change is detected. Query: find most recent message at or before target that has params attached. This is a delta/keyframe approach — avoids redundant storage while preserving full traceability. Relevant to 2a9cf71 (dynamic preset switching).","files":null}]}